§§ `The charity test applied`

-- A school with a gift shop: purposes all charitable-or-ancillary, public benefit
-- provided, no government control. MEETS THE TEST.
`Victoria College Trust` MEANS CandidateCharity WITH
    entity                                                          IS `Jersey Heritage Ltd`
    purposes                                                        IS LIST `the advancement of education`, `running a gift shop to fund the school`
    `in giving effect to those purposes, it provides (or, in the case of an applicant, provides or intends to provide) public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree`  IS TRUE
    `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons`  IS FALSE
    `its constitution expressly permits its activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by, or any of its governors to be, a person of the following description, acting in that capacity`  IS FALSE
    `(2)(a) a Minister`                                             IS FALSE
    `(2)(b) a member of the States Assembly`                        IS FALSE
    `(2)(c) any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction`  IS FALSE
    `an Order under Article 5(3) disapplies paragraph (2) in relation to this entity`  IS FALSE

#ASSERT `(a) — all of its purposes are charitable or purely ancillary` `Victoria College Trust`
#ASSERT `(b) — provides public benefit to a reasonable degree` `Victoria College Trust`
#ASSERT `Article 5(1) — the positive test` `Victoria College Trust`
#ASSERT NOT `the Article 5(2) knock-out bites` `Victoria College Trust`
#ASSERT `meets the charity test` `Victoria College Trust`

-- ONE bad purpose spoils the lot. Art 5(1)(a) says "ALL of its purposes" — so the
-- party-political purpose, however incidental it claims to be, fails the entity.
`Victoria College Trust, but campaigning` MEANS CandidateCharity WITH
    entity                                                          IS `Jersey Heritage Ltd`
    purposes                                                        IS LIST `the advancement of education`, `running a gift shop to fund the school`, `campaigning for a political party (pleaded as merely incidental)`
    `in giving effect to those purposes, it provides (or, in the case of an applicant, provides or intends to provide) public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree`  IS TRUE
    `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons`  IS FALSE
    `its constitution expressly permits its activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by, or any of its governors to be, a person of the following description, acting in that capacity`  IS FALSE
    `(2)(a) a Minister`                                             IS FALSE
    `(2)(b) a member of the States Assembly`                        IS FALSE
    `(2)(c) any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction`  IS FALSE
    `an Order under Article 5(3) disapplies paragraph (2) in relation to this entity`  IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `(a) — all of its purposes are charitable or purely ancillary` `Victoria College Trust, but campaigning`
#ASSERT NOT `Article 5(1) — the positive test` `Victoria College Trust, but campaigning`
#ASSERT NOT `meets the charity test` `Victoria College Trust, but campaigning`

-- Article 7(3)(b) — the family trust. Impeccably educational purposes, genuinely
-- funded, but it benefits only the settlor's identified children. The determiner
-- MUST NOT treat it as providing public benefit. Art 5(1)(b) fails.
`the Le Sueur Family Education Trust` MEANS CandidateCharity WITH
    entity                                                          IS `Jersey Heritage Ltd`
    purposes                                                        IS LIST `the advancement of education`
    `in giving effect to those purposes, it provides (or, in the case of an applicant, provides or intends to provide) public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree`  IS TRUE   -- so the trustees assert...
    `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons`  IS TRUE   -- ...but 7(3)(b) forbids the conclusion
    `its constitution expressly permits its activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by, or any of its governors to be, a person of the following description, acting in that capacity`  IS FALSE
    `(2)(a) a Minister`                                             IS FALSE
    `(2)(b) a member of the States Assembly`                        IS FALSE
    `(2)(c) any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction`  IS FALSE
    `an Order under Article 5(3) disapplies paragraph (2) in relation to this entity`  IS FALSE

#ASSERT `(a) — all of its purposes are charitable or purely ancillary` `the Le Sueur Family Education Trust`
#ASSERT `Article 7(3)(b) — benefits only identified natural persons` `the Le Sueur Family Education Trust`
#ASSERT NOT `(b) — provides public benefit to a reasonable degree` `the Le Sueur Family Education Trust`
#ASSERT NOT `meets the charity test` `the Le Sueur Family Education Trust`

-- Article 5(2) — the arms-length quango. Everything about it is charitable, but its
-- constitution lets the Minister direct it. The knock-out bites "DESPITE paragraph (1)".
`the Jersey Arts Quango` MEANS CandidateCharity WITH
    entity                                                          IS `Jersey Heritage Ltd`
    purposes                                                        IS LIST `the advancement of education`
    `in giving effect to those purposes, it provides (or, in the case of an applicant, provides or intends to provide) public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree`  IS TRUE
    `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons`  IS FALSE
    `its constitution expressly permits its activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by, or any of its governors to be, a person of the following description, acting in that capacity`  IS TRUE
    `(2)(a) a Minister`                                             IS TRUE
    `(2)(b) a member of the States Assembly`                        IS FALSE
    `(2)(c) any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction`  IS FALSE
    `an Order under Article 5(3) disapplies paragraph (2) in relation to this entity`  IS FALSE

-- It "OTHERWISE MEETS the charity test" — 5(1) is satisfied...
#ASSERT `Article 5(1) — the positive test` `the Jersey Arts Quango`
-- ...but 5(2) subtracts it.
#ASSERT `Article 5(2) — constitution expressly permits government direction or governorship` `the Jersey Arts Quango`
#ASSERT `the Article 5(2) knock-out bites` `the Jersey Arts Quango`
#ASSERT NOT `meets the charity test` `the Jersey Arts Quango`

-- Article 5(3) — the SAME quango, once the Minister makes an Order disapplying
-- paragraph (2) in relation to it. The defeater is itself defeated, and the entity
-- is restored to the register. Only ONE field differs from the case above.
`the Jersey Arts Quango, with an Article 5(3) Order` MEANS CandidateCharity WITH
    entity                                                          IS `Jersey Heritage Ltd`
    purposes                                                        IS LIST `the advancement of education`
    `in giving effect to those purposes, it provides (or, in the case of an applicant, provides or intends to provide) public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree`  IS TRUE
    `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons`  IS FALSE
    `its constitution expressly permits its activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by, or any of its governors to be, a person of the following description, acting in that capacity`  IS TRUE
    `(2)(a) a Minister`                                             IS TRUE
    `(2)(b) a member of the States Assembly`                        IS FALSE
    `(2)(c) any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction`  IS FALSE
    `an Order under Article 5(3) disapplies paragraph (2) in relation to this entity`  IS TRUE   -- the only change

#ASSERT `Article 5(2) — constitution expressly permits government direction or governorship` `the Jersey Arts Quango, with an Article 5(3) Order`
#ASSERT NOT `the Article 5(2) knock-out bites` `the Jersey Arts Quango, with an Article 5(3) Order`
#ASSERT `meets the charity test` `the Jersey Arts Quango, with an Article 5(3) Order`

§§ `The empty shell — the vacuous-truth corner of Article 5(1)(a)`

-- See the INTERPRETATION CALL in the header. An entity with NO purposes satisfies
-- Art 5(1)(a) VACUOUSLY ("all of its purposes are charitable" — there are none to
-- fail). It is Art 5(1)(b) that must exclude it: with no purposes, there are no
-- purposes to which it can "give effect", and so no public benefit provided in
-- consequence. The model shows the load-bearing limb clearly.
`the empty shell` MEANS CandidateCharity WITH
    entity                                                          IS `Jersey Heritage Ltd`
    purposes                                                        IS EMPTY
    `in giving effect to those purposes, it provides (or, in the case of an applicant, provides or intends to provide) public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree`  IS FALSE
    `the entity benefits only one particular natural person or a group of identified natural persons`  IS FALSE
    `its constitution expressly permits its activities to be directed or otherwise controlled by, or any of its governors to be, a person of the following description, acting in that capacity`  IS FALSE
    `(2)(a) a Minister`                                             IS FALSE
    `(2)(b) a member of the States Assembly`                        IS FALSE
    `(2)(c) any equivalent of such a person in another jurisdiction`  IS FALSE
    `an Order under Article 5(3) disapplies paragraph (2) in relation to this entity`  IS FALSE

-- 5(1)(a) is VACUOUSLY satisfied...
#ASSERT `(a) — all of its purposes are charitable or purely ancillary` `the empty shell`
-- ...and 5(1)(b) is what does the excluding.
#ASSERT NOT `(b) — provides public benefit to a reasonable degree` `the empty shell`
#ASSERT NOT `meets the charity test` `the empty shell`

§§ `The guidance duties, exercised`

-- The Commissioner publishes on day 60, inside the 90-day placeholder window.
#TRACE `Article 5(4) and 7(4) — the Commissioner's guidance duty` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Commissioner DOES `publish and maintain guidance on the charity test` AT 60

-- The full Article 5(6)-(8) chain, run to completion: consult, report, provide, lay.
#TRACE `Articles 5(6) to (8) — the consultation and laying chain` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Commissioner DOES `consult before issuing or amending guidance` AT 30
    PARTY Commissioner DOES `publish a report on the consultation` AT 50
    PARTY Commissioner DOES `provide the guidance and report to the Minister` AT 70
    PARTY Minister DOES `lay the guidance and report before the States` AT 90

-- The chain BREAKS at the last step: the Minister never lays the guidance before
-- the States. Everything upstream is fulfilled; the residual is the Minister's
-- outstanding duty, and it is BREACHED.
#TRACE `Articles 5(6) to (8) — the consultation and laying chain` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Commissioner DOES `consult before issuing or amending guidance` AT 30
    PARTY Commissioner DOES `publish a report on the consultation` AT 50
    PARTY Commissioner DOES `provide the guidance and report to the Minister` AT 70

-- Article 7(3)(a) — the determiner who DOES presume public benefit from the mere
-- fact of a charitable purpose. SHANT: doing the act IS the breach.
#TRACE `Article 7(3)(a) — no presumption of public benefit` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Commissioner DOES `presume a particular charitable purpose to be for the public benefit` AT 10
